reception precedes 1006's first activity, and every other 1860 reception is separated from the nearest prior 1006 emission by far more than a 600-unit relay could bridge (thousands of units in most cases, >800 with no evidenced intermediates in the closest case). The apparent link is attributable to hub connectivity and overall volume, not a time-respecting chain."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Endpoint structure.** In the window, 1006 has only 6 events (5 distinct out-partners: 45, 230, 925, 1532, 1680) and 1860 has only 6 events (5 distinct in-partners: 153, 182, 743, 958, 1390) \u2014 both are low-degree nodes despite the window containing ~6,900 events over 1,936 nodes (step_01, step_02, step_04, step_05).\n\n**No 2-hop bridge.** The out-set of 1006 and the in-set of 1860 are disjoint, so any cascade requires \u22653 hops. A static path does exist (1006\u219245\u2192153\u21921860; edges 45\u2013153 and 45\u2013182 appear in the 2-hop neighbourhood, step_03), and 153/182/958 are high-traffic hubs (step_06) \u2014 this is exactly the \"connection when time is ignored / hub popularity\" confounder the task warns about.\n\n**Temporal placement.** Binary-searching the emission/reception times:\n- 1006's events localize to \u2248[20432,20831], [20832,21231], [21232,22831], [36432,37231], [41232,42031], [46832,50031] (steps 07, 09, 11, 13, 15).\n- 1860's events localize to \u2248[20032,20431], [24432,27631], two in [30832,34031], [37232,38031], [42832,43631] (steps 08, 10, 12, 14, 16).\n\n1860's first reception (~20032\u201320431) *precedes* 1006's earliest activity (~20432+), so it cannot be downstream. The remaining 1860 receptions in [24432,27631] and [30832,34031] are separated from any prior 1006 event by thousands of time units \u2014 far beyond a 600-unit relay chain. The only marginally close pairings are 1006@[36432,37231] \u2192 1860@[37232,38031] and 1006@[41232,42031] \u2192 1860@[42832,43631]; the latter's minimum separation (~801) already exceeds one hop and would need \u22652 intermediate events that are not evidenced, and the former would require a 3-hop relay through 45\u2192153 for which no intervening events were located. No verified chain of \u2264600-unit steps links the two.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8eb05c06\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.58,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1006 and 1860 are connected only when time is ignored (via hubs 45/153/182), and their out/in neighbourhoods are disjoint, so any cascade needs at least three hops. Temporal localization shows 1860's earliest reception precedes 1006's first activity, and every other 1860 reception is separated from the nearest prior 1006 emission by far more than a 600-unit relay could bridge (thousands of units in most cases, >800 with no evidenced intermediates in the closest case). The apparent link is attributable to hub connectivity and overall volume, not a time-respecting chain.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 53749, "total_output_tokens": 13026, "total_tokens": 66775, "total_latency_ms": 176202, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}